# ---
#
# This file is expected to cover the editor messages, including controls, notifications, etc. (but not nodes)
# and may be used as a foundation to create new translations for other languages. As a convention,
# for general messages and those short (in english), the original values are kept as keys
# (~ untranslated); otherwise UPPER_CASE keys would be used for brevity and precision.
#
# For nodes, check out their respective translations sub-directories.
#
# NOTE:
# + Tags like `%s` and mustache `{placeholders}` are mostly for formatting purposes and shall be kept as they are to allow proper replacement.
# + A particular world or phrase may have been used in multiple modules, identically, and to avoid duplicates, only listed in one section, most-likely the topmost/first one.
# + The messages commented out (and being marked with a preceding `# !` attribute) are likely to be UI fillers and replaced by scripts, so there may not be any need for them to be translated.
#
# ---

